# Byte-exact line endings for anything that is embedded into a shell, executed
# as a POSIX script, or compared byte-for-byte by a test.
#
# The two bundled Zsh plugins are compiled into the binary with `include_str!`
# and later written to the user's config directory, so a CRLF checkout would
# ship a broken plugin on Windows. The prompt snapshots are compared verbatim
# against generated output, which always uses LF.
*.sh                                      text eol=lf
*.zsh                                     text eol=lf
scripts/install.sh                        text eol=lf
crates/kiseki-compiler/tests/snapshots/** text eol=lf
tests/snapshots/**                        text eol=lf
